# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#    test/lsan.supp                                                           #
#                                                                             #
#    The suppressions of LeakSanitizer for the tests, which ctest passes in   #
#    LSAN_OPTIONS when the build has -fsanitize=address [see                  #
#    test/CMakeLists.txt]; by hand: LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=test/lsan.supp. #
#    Each pattern drops a leak whose stack passes through a library that      #
#    keeps memory until the process ends by design, not through ADS.          #
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

# Open MPI, its components (in the thread of libevent too) and hwloc, which
# MPI_Init sets up and never frees
leak:MPI_Init
leak:ompi_mpi_init
leak:orte_init
leak:libmpi.so
leak:libopen-pal.so
leak:libopen-rte.so
leak:libevent_core
leak:event_base_loop

# FastFlow, whose farms allocate the mutex and the condition of their
# blocking mode and never free them
leak:ff::ff_loadbalancer::init_input_blocking

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
